-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Robin of the Wood
  Publisher   Odin, 1985
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Robin of the Wood (1985)(Odin Computer Graphics)[128K].z80
  MD5         d2fa7f2eeb8ccb75c30edbacb432a8b5

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Changes     1.1: Starts on a Next: the game's stack sits in the printer
              buffer, which the loader overwrites; it is now put back before
              the game runs

  Note        Robin, the outlaws, the guards and the creatures are hardware
              sprites, so they no longer take the colours of the forest they
              walk through; the scenery and the panel stay as the game draws
              them. The 128K release, with its music. Proven on three recorded
              journeys; an Enhanced colour set comes later. About 2% slower
              than the original in busy scenes.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite energy

  Infinite energy from the archive .pok's 128K line, its second POKE moved to
  bank 0 where the game reads it; proved in replay: energy stayed at 15
  through a 6,188-frame life cycle (13 decrements without it). The archive's
  flowers and money cheat writes one address twice and is left out.

